[TITLE]
AquaOptima dPHM-PINN Sprint 16 — small reference EPANET .inp fixture
in US-customary units with a throttle-control valve (TCV).
Three-node topology:

    R1 (suction reservoir, fixed head 165 ft)
      |
      +-- V1 (TCV, K = 2.5, 6 in) --> J1 (elev 0, no consumer)
                                          |
                                          +-- P1 (pipe, 660 ft, 6 in)
                                                |
                                                +-> J2 (200 GPM consumer)

The Sprint 16 fallback parser converts the GPM/ft/in inputs to SI
through the EpanetUnitSystem manifest before routing the TCV row
through the conservative resistance surrogate
``fit_tcv_resistance_surrogate``. TCV setting K is dimensionless and
is *not* scaled by the unit system. Solvable by
aquaoptima.dphm.newton_solve with jacobian_mode="analytic".

[JUNCTIONS]
;ID   Elev   Demand   Pattern
 J1   0.0      0.0    ;     ; TCV discharge node (no consumer)
 J2   0.0    200.0    ;     ; 200 GPM consumer

[RESERVOIRS]
;ID   Head   Pattern
 R1   165.0  ;          ; 165 ft fixed-head suction reservoir

[PIPES]
;ID   Node1   Node2   Length   Diameter   Roughness   MinorLoss   Status
 P1   J1      J2      660.0    6.0        130.0       0.0         OPEN

[VALVES]
;ID   Node1   Node2   Diameter   Type   Setting   MinorLoss
 V1   R1      J1      6.0        TCV    2.5       0

[OPTIONS]
 Units                GPM
 Headloss             H-W

[END]
